    "body": "Installed via Scoop https://scoop.sh/\r\n\r\nThis might have been a weird situation. I had just re-installed Windows via the \"Reset My PC\" option. That removed all installed application programs -- but did not touch my `$HOME` dir.\r\n\r\nScoop installs (almost) everything to a self-contained directory tree at `${HOME}/scoop`, seems to be like Homebrew on macOS.\r\n\r\nIt could be that if I were to truly start fresh, I would have re-installed Starship via `scoop install starship`. I did not do that, did not run any installation procedure, as the files and config info were already there, in my `${HOME}/scoop`...\r\n\r\nHmm. I can take a look at that, do a proper re-install, see if it picks up the VC runtime dependency.",
